        '19424',
        'SAP BO requirments (data modling) - Closed ticket',
        'Dear Team,  Since are required from us evidences of below practices, can you provide us with the available document like ( business glossary,meta data documents , data profiling, data quality process....etc) as you can see below  regards    APO14-Managed Data  1. Develop a clear strategy for managing data effectively across the bank and ensure communicating the data management strategy to all stakeholders.  2. Clarify who is responsible for managing and governing data to ensure accountability.  3. Develop an Implementation plan for data management strategy.  4. Build and create a business glossary of key terms to ensure consistent understanding of data across teams. 1-Ensure that standard business terms are readily available and communicated to relevant stakeholders.2-Ensure that each business term added to the business glossary has a unique name and unique definition.3-Use standard industry business terms and definitions, as appropriate, in the business glossary.  5. Document Metadata  6. Develop a Data Quality Strategy to ensure data is accurate, reliable, and meets business needs.  7. Set up a process for tracking and reporting issues with data quality. Establish improvement plans to correct the data quality issues.  8. Establish consistent Data Profiling methodologies, processes, practices, tools, and results templates.  9. Ensure that policies mandate management of data history, including retention, destruction and audit trail requirements.  10.Ensure the existence of a defined method that guarantees accessibility to the historical data necessary to support business needs.  11. Define a schedule to ensure correct backup of all critical data.   12. Define requirements for on-site and off-site storage of backup data, taking into account volume, capacity and retention period, in alignment with the business requirements.  13. Establish a testing schedule for backup data. Ensure that the data can be restored correctly without drastically impacting business.  14. Measure the KPIs as per their defined frequency.',
