(
        '19399',
        'VAs Q3-2025 - Study',
        'Please note that the attached VAs are located on server 172.20.17.89,172.20.17.88 172.20.17.85 , 172.20.17.86 . We would appreciate your urgent support to resolve VAs',
        'Dear Bilal    - SAP BusinessObjects BI 4.3 does not use Apache Commons FileUpload as part of its core web platform.  The official SAP fixed vulnerability lists for BA 4.2 / 4.3 and newer platforms do not include CVE 2025 48976 among addressed issues    - SAP BusinessObjects 4.3 does not depend on Apache Tomcat for its core application server. Instead, it uses proprietary or supported Java application servers (e.g., Tomcat, WebSphere, WebLogic) only when explicitly deployed in those environments.  The official SAP Security Patch Notes for June 2025 (which include CVE 2025 42988) do not mention CVE 2025 48988 as affecting SAP BO 4.3    - The default SAP BO deployment does not rely on the Apache Tomcat installer—particularly the Windows installer—for core components.  There is no reference to CVE 2025 49124 in the official SAP security notes for SAP BO 4.3 or BI Platform as of July 2025 .  Therefore, standard SAP BO installations are not exposed to this vulnerability, unless Tomcat was installed or upgraded manually using the vulnerable installer binaries.    - SAP BusinessObjects 4.3 default stack does not rely on Apache Tomcat''s pre-release versions for the web application layer.  SAP installs BO on supported application servers (such as Tomcat, WebSphere, WebLogic) but only in stable, patched versions.  There are no references to CVE 2025 49125 in official SAP security notes or patches for BO 4.3 or BI platform components   Therefore, standard BO deployments are not exposed to this vulnerability—unless you have manually installed a vulnerable Tomcat version.    Regarding Plugin 65057  The bank team must apply the same security permission/ policy that has been applied on server 88 on the mentioned path.',
        '2025-08-03T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
        '2025-08-05T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
