        '19507',
        'Upgrade without delay to Apache Tomcat 9.0.106 or later',
        'Upgrade without delay to Apache Tomcat 9.0.106 or later',
        'Reference to the mentioned vulnerabilities kindly find below recommended solutions :    - Upgrade SAP BO to 4.3 sp5 patch1  - Configure SSL over tomcat and IIS ,Create and apply new CA certificate based on the server FQDN  - Set X-Frame-Options: DENY on HTTP Response Headers on IIS  - set max file upload to 30 MB In server.xml, adjust the connector setting: <Connector port="8080" maxPostSize="31457280" />  - Close port 8080 for Tomcat and 80 for IIS and keep port 8443 for tomcat and 443 for IIS functioning.  - apply below tags on web.xml to resolve HTTP detect vulnerability on Tomcat.  Insert the following code into your web.xml file, placing it just before the closing ''</web-app>'' tag:  <filter>   <filter-name>httpHeaderSecurity</filter-name>   <filter-class>org.apache.catalina.filters.HttpHeaderSecurityFilter</filter-class>   <init-param>   <param-name>hstsMaxAgeSeconds</param-name>   <param-value>31536000</param-value>   </init-param>   <async-supported>true</async-supported>  </filter>  <filter-mapping>   <filter-name>httpHeaderSecurity</filter-name>   <url-pattern>/*</url-pattern>   <dispatcher>REQUEST</dispatcher>  </filter-mapping>',
        '2025-08-17T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
