        'Ticket status as of 27-Aug-2025:    Dear Mohammad,    Kindly be informed that the facility for the provided contract is a revolving loan. Currently, the status of this loan in the murabaha table in banks is marked as closed (MURABAHA_STA = 5). However, in the bank''s facility table, the status is suspended (STA_CODE = 4), which should indicate that the facility is still open and not closed.    Additionally, the risk limit value for this loan is (0), even though there is still an outstanding reduction limit of 4,999,999.997 on the loan.  Therefore, I kindly request your clarification on the following points:  •Why is this loan considered closed while it is suspended, and should still be treated as active?  •Why did every closed loan risk limit change to (0) upon closing the facility?  •Could you please share the business point of view regarding the above, considering that this loan is still being retrieved as active in the BankBI data warehouse, based on the criteria you had previously provided during the project?  Regarding the number_unpaid_due_installments, please find the requested Excel sheet on the following path on the application production server:    C:\Users\Administrator\Desktop\NUMBER OF UNPAID INSTALLMENTS.xlsx    Best Regards,',
