(
        '19797',
        'Crif balance source',
        ', as the attached email, the Outstanding Balance is showing as 0, while in the file extracted from the Credit Bureau it clearly shows a balance greater than 0 for the same contract.    Could you please clarify from which source/field CRIF is retrieving the Outstanding Balance value in your process?    This will help us understand the discrepancy between the Credit Bureau file and the output you shared.',
        'Dear Mohammad,    Please find below the details of how OUTSTANDING_BALANCE is derived and the source mappings used in the data warehouse.    1- The OUTSANDING_BALANCE column reads from below the data warehouse criteria    ABS( ((PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.USED_AMT + ISNULL(PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.PROFIT_BAL,0)) - ABS( ISNULL(PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.UNPAID_DUE_INSTALLMENTS_AMOUNT,0 )) ) ) OUTSTANDING_BALANCE     2- The column PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.USED_AMT from the datawarehouse reads from the core table FAC_DETL column USED_AMT.    3- The column PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.PROFIT_BAL from the data warehouse reads from the following core query (Column profit):  SELECT A.BRA_CODE,   A.CUS_NUM,   A.CUR_CODE,   A.LED_CODE,   A.SUB_ACCT_CODE,   A.REF_TYPE,   A.REF_YEAR,   A.REF_NUM,   B.FAC_REF_KEY,   SUM (A.REVENUE_AMT) PROFIT   FROM IJAR_PAY A, IJAR_TAB B   WHERE A.BRA_CODE = B.BRA_CODE   AND A.CUS_NUM = B.CUS_NUM   AND A.CUR_CODE = B.CUR_CODE   AND A.LED_CODE = B.LED_CODE   AND A.SUB_ACCT_CODE = B.SUB_ACCT_CODE   AND A.REF_TYPE = B.REF_TYPE   AND A.REF_YEAR = B.REF_YEAR   AND A.REF_NUM = B.REF_NUM   --AND A.CUS_NUM = ''35593''   AND A.INS_STA = 1   AND A.MAT_DATE <= B.PER_END_DATE ---''25-JUL-2024''  GROUP BY A.BRA_CODE,   A.CUS_NUM,   A.CUR_CODE,   A.LED_CODE,   A.SUB_ACCT_CODE,   A.REF_TYPE,   A.REF_YEAR,   A.REF_NUM,   B.FAC_REF_KEY  UNION ALL    SELECT A.BRA_CODE,   A.CUS_NUM,   A.CUR_CODE,   A.LED_CODE,   A.SUB_ACCT_CODE,   A.REF_TYPE,   A.REF_YEAR,   A.REF_NUM,   B.FAC_REF_KEY,   SUM (A.PROFIT_AMT) PROFIT   FROM MUR_PAY A, MUR_TAB B   WHERE A.BRA_CODE = B.BRA_CODE   AND A.CUS_NUM = B.CUS_NUM   AND A.CUR_CODE = B.CUR_CODE   AND A.LED_CODE = B.LED_CODE   AND A.SUB_ACCT_CODE = B.SUB_ACCT_CODE   AND A.REF_TYPE = B.REF_TYPE   AND A.REF_YEAR = B.REF_YEAR   AND A.REF_NUM = B.REF_NUM   --AND A.CUS_NUM = ''54704''   AND A.INS_STA = 1  GROUP BY A.BRA_CODE,   A.CUS_NUM,   A.CUR_CODE,   A.LED_CODE,   A.SUB_ACCT_CODE,   A.REF_TYPE,   A.REF_YEAR,   A.REF_NUM,   B.FAC_REF_KEY    4- The column PIO_RISK_PORTFOLIO.UNPAID_DUE_INSTALLMENTS_AMOUNT from the data warehouse calculate by applying this criteria decode( UNPAID_DUE_INSTALLMENTS_AMOUNT < 1, 1, UNPAID_DUE_INSTALLMENTS_AMOUNT ) , noting that the column UNPAID_DUE_INSTALLMENTS reads from the below core query:    (SELECT SUM ( INS_BAL + ARREARS_BAL ) --(REVENUE_AMT + DEP_AMT)   FROM IJAR_PAY A   WHERE IJAR_PAY.BRA_CODE = A.BRA_CODE   AND IJAR_PAY.CUS_NUM = A.CUS_NUM   AND IJAR_PAY.CUR_CODE = A.CUR_CODE   AND IJAR_PAY.LED_CODE = A.LED_CODE   AND IJAR_PAY.SUB_ACCT_CODE = A.SUB_ACCT_CODE   AND IJAR_PAY.REF_TYPE = A.REF_TYPE   AND IJAR_PAY.REF_YEAR = A.REF_YEAR   AND IJAR_PAY.REF_NUM = A.REF_NUM   AND INS_STA IN (2, 3, 7)) unpaid_due_installments_amount,    5- The contract number 059022000003 outstanding balance is as follows:           Best Regards,',
        '2025-09-11T00:00:00.000Z'::timestamptz,
