        '19848',
        'AML Watchlist Checker issue',
        'Dear Support Team,  FastPay AML officers (Gazang Hamad and Eman Braeem) encountered an issue: they are unable to access the AML Watchlist Checker module. The system displays a “You are not authorized” error when they attempt to open it (Figure 1).  What I checked:  •I browsed in Admin Panel > Administration > Define Access Right > Update Access Right.(figure 2)  •Verified that their profile (AML Officer) still has the same access rights that previously allowed them to use this function.  Temporary Fix Applied:  •I solved the issue by going to Assign Access Rights and re-assigning the AML Officer Access Right Name to the users.(figure 3)  •This allowed them to regain access.  New Issue Identified:  •After reassigning, I noticed a new error message appearing: “Your license are expired Please reactivate” (figure 4).  Request for Support:  1.Please confirm why the original access rights stopped working, even though the role permissions were unchanged.  2.Assist in resolving the new license expiration issue so AML officers can continue their work without interruption. ( note the license expired red note is not MS windows issue !)  3.Kindly advise if additional reactivation steps or patches are required.  Thank you for your prompt suppor',
        'Dears,    Based on our web session, please note the following updates:    1. Permissions Issue: Permissions had stopped working due to a new rule added to the Bank BI parameter. This caused some users to lose access. The parameter type has now been adjusted, and everything is functioning as expected.    2. License Issue: After the update, the license was removed by default. It has now been re-activated and is functioning as expected. You can verify this on your side.    Kindly review the points above and confirm so we can proceed to close this ticket.',
